in @prism

in @mirror/glass/ast/shape

# @mirror/glass/ast/shape/fixed — the `fixed` shape variant: a
# module-top binding that is fully settled, content-addressed, and
# carries no holes or inference.
#
# Per the per-variant file pattern declared in @mirror/glass/ast/
# shape: variants of `shape` may land in their own sub-file when
# they want to declare structure of their own. `fixed` does — it
# is the substrate's first keyword declared not by hand-coding a
# new token in the bootstrap, but by aliasing an existing Prism op
# at the substrate altitude.
#
# `type fixed = settle`
#
# Reads: the `fixed` shape variant IS the `settle` Prism op,
# applied at the binding altitude. Same operation; substrate-
# altitude name. The bootstrap does not learn a new keyword;
# the substrate accumulates one. Every property the substrate
# already knows about `settle` (settled construction, monad
# laws, content-addressing) transfers to `fixed` by alias.
#
# Per Alex 2026-05-26: *"`fixed`. Like `const`. But math. And a
# `fixed` value cannot include any holes. No inference. It needs
# to be a fully settled crystal. Becomes content addressed."*
#
# Properties of `fixed` (inherited via the alias):
#
#   - Cannot contain holes (`\`) — settle requires settled construction
#   - Cannot contain `@fate` inference — settled at compile time
#   - Must be a fully settled crystal — the monad laws guarantee it
#   - Content-addressed on declaration — the OID is the binding
#
# Distinction from `beam` (body-altitude, dynamic):
#
#   - `beam x = expr` inside a lambda body: dynamic; carries Beam<T>
#     metadata; may contain holes or inference; subject to spectral
#     measurement; lifted to `fixed` by
#     @kintsugi/fracture/dynamic-beam-to-fixed when holonomy settles.
#   - `fixed x = expr` at module-top: static; fully settled;
#     content-addressed; the OID IS the binding.
#
# Migration source for legacy `settle <name> = <combinator>`
# bindings: @kintsugi/fracture/settle-to-fixed.
#
# Insight: docs/insights/2026-05-26-fixed-and-the-spectral-feedback-fracture.md

grammar @mirror/glass/ast/shape/fixed {
  # The substrate's declaration that the `fixed` keyword aliases
  # the `settle` Prism op. No body needed — the alias IS the
  # declaration. Every downstream substrate that mentions `fixed`
  # resolves through this line to the settle Prism op at the
  # binding altitude.
  type fixed = settle
}

out fixed
out @mirror/glass/ast/shape/fixed
